From: Julian Bouzas <julian.bouzas@collabora.com>
Subject: [PATCH] alsa: backport the opt-out for Pro Audio profile probing

Backport of upstream a8b9ce2050dfb3f91c19061562d0a161117c3ab8:
https://github.com/PipeWire/pipewire/commit/a8b9ce2050dfb3f91c19061562d0a161117c3ab8

PipeWire 1.0.5 unconditionally probes every PCM for its Pro Audio profile,
even when a valid UCM profile already limits ordinary HiFi to one PCM.
Allow the specific device to opt out with api.acp.disable-pro-audio.
Default behavior for other cards is unchanged. The G955N rule enables it
only for the Exynos8895-Madera primary card.

Adaptation to 1.0.5: place property parsing beside pro-channels, before the
later split-enable property existed. Build against the exact Ubuntu source
including its existing distribution/security patches, not vanilla 1.0.5.

diff --git a/spa/plugins/alsa/acp/acp.c b/spa/plugins/alsa/acp/acp.c
--- a/spa/plugins/alsa/acp/acp.c
+++ b/spa/plugins/alsa/acp/acp.c
@@ -470,7 +470,8 @@
 	ap->profile.flags = ACP_PROFILE_OFF;
 	pa_hashmap_put(impl->profiles, ap->name, ap);
 
-	add_pro_profile(impl, impl->card.index);
+	if (!impl->disable_pro_audio)
+		add_pro_profile(impl, impl->card.index);
 
 	PA_HASHMAP_FOREACH(ap, impl->profile_set->profiles, state) {
 		pa_alsa_mapping *m;
@@ -1607,6 +1608,8 @@
 			impl->rate = atoi(s);
 		if ((s = acp_dict_lookup(props, "api.acp.pro-channels")) != NULL)
 			impl->pro_channels = atoi(s);
+		if ((s = acp_dict_lookup(props, "api.acp.disable-pro-audio")) != NULL)
+			impl->disable_pro_audio = spa_atob(s);
 	}
 
 	impl->ucm.default_sample_spec.format = PA_SAMPLE_S16NE;
diff --git a/spa/plugins/alsa/acp/card.h b/spa/plugins/alsa/acp/card.h
--- a/spa/plugins/alsa/acp/card.h
+++ b/spa/plugins/alsa/acp/card.h
@@ -47,6 +47,7 @@
 	bool auto_profile;
 	bool auto_port;
 	bool ignore_dB;
+	bool disable_pro_audio;
 	uint32_t rate;
 	uint32_t pro_channels;
 
